declare name "Repeat Loop Library";
declare version "0.2.0";
declare author "faust-diff";
declare license "MIT";

//################################## repeat.lib ##########################################
// Repeat loop library. Its official prefix is `rp`.
//
// A library simulation of the `repeat` primitive of faust-rs
// (`docs/repeat-note-en.md`): a bounded loop whose exit is decided inside.
//
// ```
// repeat(C) : n + 1 -> m      for C : n -> m + 1
// ```
//
// The first input is the clock `H`, the bound: the body runs at most
// `int(H)` times per outer sample, and again after an iteration only while
// the last output of `C`, the continue flag, was non-zero. The first
// iteration is unconditional when `H > 0`; `H = 0` holds the outputs. Local
// time inside `C` counts executed iterations; the inputs are snapshotted at
// the sample.
//
// Built on the two clock-domain primitives that exist: an outer integer
// `ondemand` runs `H` times per sample; inside it, a boolean `ondemand` runs
// the body on the first iteration of the sample (the sample index passed
// in changes) and then while the flag held from the previous iteration is
// non-zero. This is the form of section 1.5 of the faust-rs plan
// `porting/repeat-counted-loop-with-exit-analysis-and-plan-2026-09-18-en.md`,
// measured there against the semantics; the primitive, when it lands,
// replaces it without changing a sample.
//
// The library uses `basics.lib` and `signals.lib` through `stdfaust.lib`,
// so the directory of the Faust standard libraries must be on the import
// path. It is a `faust-rs` library: `ondemand` is not known to the C++
// Faust compiler. Names are in snake_case.
//
// The Repeat library is organized into 1 section:
//
// * [Bounded Loop](#bounded-loop)
//
// It should be used using the `rp` environment:
//
// ```
// rp = library("repeat.lib");
// process = (H, inputs) : rp.repeat(body);
// ```
//
// #### References
//
// * <https://github.com/grame-cncm/faust-rs/blob/main/docs/repeat-note-en.md>
// * <https://github.com/sletz/faust-diff-ts808> (README §2: the simulation
//   and its cost)
//########################################################################################

import("stdfaust.lib");

//==================================== Bounded Loop ======================================
// The one function of the library: a body run a bounded number of times per
// sample, with an exit the body decides.
//========================================================================================

//-----------------------------------`(rp.)repeat`----------------------------------------
// Run the body `C` at most `int(H)` times per sample, stopping after an
// iteration whose continue flag, the last output of `C`, is zero. The
// first iteration of a sample is unconditional when `H > 0`; `H = 0` holds
// the outputs of the previous sample. Inside `C`, time counts executed
// iterations across samples, and the inputs are those of the sample; a
// body that must restart at every sample reads the sample index as an
// input (`ba.time + 1` passed in the bus) and resets its state when it
// changes, as in the example. The outputs are the first `m` outputs of the
// last executed iteration, held until the next.
//
// #### Usage
//
// ```
// (H, si.bus(n)) : repeat(C) : si.bus(m)
// ```
//
// Where:
//
// * `C`: the body, `n` inputs and `m + 1` outputs, the last one the
//   continue flag (non-zero to run again)
// * `H`: the bound, the largest number of iterations of a sample (a signal;
//   `0` skips the sample)
//
// #### Example
//
// The square root of the input by Newton's method, at most 8 steps per
// sample, stopping when a step is under 1e-9: the sample index tells the
// first iteration, where the estimate is reset to the input.
//
// ```
// rp = library("repeat.lib");
// import("stdfaust.lib");
// newton(t, a) = iter ~ _
// with {
//     first = t != t';
//     iter(y) = yn, (abs(yn - y0) > 1e-9)
//     with {
//         y0 = select2(first, y, a);
//         yn = 0.5 * (y0 + a / y0);
//     };
// };
// process(a) = (8, ba.time + 1, a) : rp.repeat(newton);
// ```
//
// #### Test
// ```
// rp = library("repeat.lib");
// ba = library("basics.lib");
// repeat_test = (8, ba.time + 1, 2.0) : rp.repeat(newton)
// with {
//     newton(t, a) = iter ~ _
//     with {
//         first = t != t';
//         iter(y) = yn, (abs(yn - y0) > 1e-9)
//         with {
//             y0 = select2(first, y, a);
//             yn = 0.5 * (y0 + a / y0);
//         };
//     };
// };
// ```
//
// #### References
//
// * <https://github.com/grame-cncm/faust-rs/blob/main/docs/repeat-note-en.md>
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
declare repeat license "MIT";
repeat(C) = (_, (ba.time + 1, si.bus(n))) : ondemand(shell)
with {
    n = inputs(C);
    m = outputs(C) - 1;
    shell = (first, si.bus(n)) : (gate ~ (si.block(m), _)) : (si.bus(m), !)
    with {
        first = _ <: (_ != _');
        gate = ((_, _) : |), si.bus(n) : ondemand(C);
    };
};
